From: OpenWrt
Subject: tools: drop obsolete bundled getline for Apple hosts

The host tools pull in a bundled getline implementation under #ifdef
__APPLE__, but neither tools/getline.h nor tools/getline.c exist in this
tree. Modern macOS provides getline() via <stdio.h> (POSIX-2008), so the
includes are unnecessary and only break the build when compiling the host
tools on a macOS build host (Linux build hosts never define __APPLE__).

This should be fixed upstream as well.

--- a/tools/os_support.h
+++ b/tools/os_support.h
@@ -28,8 +28,4 @@
 #include "mingw_support.h"
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __APPLE__
-#include "getline.h"
-#endif
-
 #endif /* __OS_SUPPORT_H_ */
--- a/tools/os_support.c
+++ b/tools/os_support.c
@@ -23,6 +23,3 @@
 #ifdef __MINGW32__
 #include "mingw_support.c"
 #endif
-#ifdef __APPLE__
-#include "getline.c"
-#endif
